From 052129ae5b7e072513b80ac2626d82792e6a8463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:28:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: stop reading a setting value at an unexpected character

borg_proc_setting() skips spaces and '=' after a setting name, then
reads the value.  For an integer setting it only advanced past '-' or
stopped at a digit; any other character (a word such as 'off', or a
setting name with extra letters such as 'borg_stop_dlevelx 5') was
never consumed, so the loop spun forever and the game hung at start-up
while reading borg.txt.

Stop at any other character and keep the setting's default value, as a
boolean setting already does.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#141.

(cherry picked from commit 45dfc9b1f4930b28841d0c38b73cc4cd3171aab0)
---
 src/borg/borg-init.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-init.c b/src/borg/borg-init.c
index 59be9fac9..808263230 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-init.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-init.c
@@ -141,6 +141,9 @@ static bool borg_proc_setting(
                 break;
             }
         }
+
+        /* anything else is not a value: keep the default */
+        break;
     }
 
     if (negative)
-- 
2.53.0

